                        "tags": [
                            "plural"
                        ],
                        "form": "beatniks"
                    },
                    {
                        "form_id": "e8267ed4-4c96-4ff2-b898-05aed4f4abb6",
                        "entry_id": "45fe422a-940b-3f42-800c-93c2cf4fdc17",
                        "tags": [
                            "plural",
                            "rare"
                        ],
                        "form": "beatniki"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "a68e1ec1-41e6-3537-aee3-4f0228ee2a41",
                        "entry_id": "45fe422a-940b-3f42-800c-93c2cf4fdc17",
                        "glosses": [
                            "A person who dresses in a manner that is not socially acceptable and is supposed to reject conventional norms of thought and behavior; nonconformist in dress and behavior."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "96d13258-6845-415f-9d4a-bcbca561171b",
                                "sense_id": "a68e1ec1-41e6-3537-aee3-4f0228ee2a41",
                                "text": "The drive against the stilyagi has hampered but not destroyed the development of (Soviet-style) “beatniki” among the younger artistic and literary intelligentsia. […] The tendency of Soviet “beatniki” is to emulate what they consider the Left-Bank bohemianism of Paris. It is a faint whisper of a similar movement among young East European intellectuals, particularly in Poland, to make ultrasophistication their mark of separateness from “proletarian” society."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "79f4470e-c306-34ba-af0d-5333a6191f8c",
                        "entry_id": "45fe422a-940b-3f42-800c-93c2cf4fdc17",
                        "glosses": [
                            "A person associated with the Beat Generation of the 1950s and 1960s or its style."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "1c97ea6b-4f99-42be-b06a-f92f9220dfa9",
                                "sense_id": "79f4470e-c306-34ba-af0d-5333a6191f8c",
                                "text": "The Beatles first surfaced in the USSR in 1964, when the style of dress of the ‘Beatniki’ was enthusiastically copied."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "c555be76-aba1-4a10-8f76-759598ad8276",
                                "sense_id": "79f4470e-c306-34ba-af0d-5333a6191f8c",
                                "text": "Worrying news from the west upset Soviet authorities even further. Punk rock was already causing trouble in Poland and other east-European countries. Did someone in the administration fear a repetition of Beatlemania, with decent, twist-dancing beatniki being replaced by pogo-dancing, sneering and gobbing impersonators of Johnny Rotten?"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "c95fddc7-dcd3-4bdc-913c-7eba1fb77578",
                                "sense_id": "79f4470e-c306-34ba-af0d-5333a6191f8c",
                                "text": "In tight black jeans and black polo-neck sweater he reminded her of an old-fashioned beatnik."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "a2795a2a-4217-4931-a90e-5ed05b35daff",
                        "source_entry_id": "45fe422a-940b-3f42-800c-93c2cf4fdc17",
                        "source_sense_description": "beatnik",
                        "target_lang_word": "beatník",
                        "target_lang_code": "cs",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": []
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "9f07a66e-5054-4b31-adf3-3e8b7f5bce38",
                        "source_entry_id": "45fe422a-940b-3f42-800c-93c2cf4fdc17",
                        "source_sense_description": "beatnik",
                        "target_lang_word": "beatnik",
                        "target_lang_code": "fr",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "beatnik",
                                "target_lang_code": "fr",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "e79cc800-c900-3637-ad32-5e3590c58911",
                                        "entry_id": "e4419b3a-c271-3a27-a002-58bbd5025ad6",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Membre de la Beat Generation, mouvement littéraire et artistique né dans les années 1950, aux États-Unis."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "33a991f7-6dfd-4a18-bb99-e8b5283fef71",
                                                "sense_id": "e79cc800-c900-3637-ad32-5e3590c58911",
                                                "text": "Deuxièmement, j'aurais affirmé que ce que nous appelons en Amérique les hippies et que vous appelez les beatniks constitue la nouvelle classe révolutionnaire. Je n'ai jamais rien prétendu de ce genre."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "53559062-8161-46b9-96b7-3604f3ad7d0a",
                                                "sense_id": "e79cc800-c900-3637-ad32-5e3590c58911",
                                                "text": "C'était le rendez-vous des babs, des routards, des beatniks en partance pour les Indes. Les minibus se garaient en face."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "bbfa57e4-c4ac-4cd5-85c8-a9bb72157b46",
                                                "sense_id": "e79cc800-c900-3637-ad32-5e3590c58911",
                                                "text": "– Voilà, barrez-vous, beatniks !\n– C’est ça ! Oust ! Bande de misérables ! ajoute Blondin, depuis le bar, pour faire bonne mesure."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "baa2b80f-79ed-4b2a-b8c9-8c27f5b9959d",
                        "source_entry_id": "45fe422a-940b-3f42-800c-93c2cf4fdc17",
                        "source_sense_description": "beatnik",
                        "target_lang_word": "Beatnik",
                        "target_lang_code": "de",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "Beatnik",
